    "local": "Use case: scientific-educational. Create one independent hypothetical local landscape on Hydra, Pluto's small irregular moon, wide 16:9 approximately 1672 by 941. Photorealistic scientific illustration of independently invented pale grey fine-grained regolith with scattered angular blocks, shallow irregular depressions and a low uneven broken horizon. Subtle brighter ice-like patches are artistic suggestions, not measured composition, crystalline grains, chemical fractions or observed local deposits. Low oblique illumination, grey colour and exposure are assumptions. Almost black empty sky is assumed transparency, not measured absence of an atmosphere. This is NOT a reconstruction of a New Horizons photograph, LORRI pixel blocks, any observed crater, or a mapped site. No permanent Pluto-facing location: Hydra rotates rapidly. No Sun, planets, stars, astronomical disks, haze, plumes, liquids, oceans, biology, people, spacecraft, structures or survivable landing. Do not use, recolour or copy any Moon, Mars, Pluto, Charon, Nix, asteroid or other observed body's surface map. No reference images. Legible unobtrusive footer exactly 'IMAGINED · LOCAL HYDRA'; smaller line 'Terrain, materials and lighting are assumed'. Sober natural grey palette, independently composed terrain.",
    "sky": "Use case: scientific-educational. Create one independent hypothetical sky view from Hydra, Pluto's rapidly rotating small irregular moon. Wide 16:9 about 1672x941. Foreground independently invented grey regolith, angular blocks, shallow depressions and irregular low horizon, lower half. Black empty sky, assumed transparency not measured atmospheric absence. Two SMALL separated disks above horizon: Pluto about 31 pixels diameter at this canvas size, Charon about 15 pixels; do not enlarge for drama. Pluto muted grey beige subtly mottled, Charon grey; their patterns, colours, phase and exposure independently invented, no copying observed maps. These are undated illustrative barycentric distances at 90 degree HFOV, not a registered site or permanent Pluto-facing hemisphere. Small bright crescent or partly lit disks with restrained exposure, no stars, Sun, rings, foreground atmosphere, haze, plume, liquids, ocean, biology, people, spacecraft, structures or survivable landing. Do not copy/recolour Moon/Mars/Pluto/Charon/Nix/asteroid terrain or any actual photograph. No reference images. Legible unobtrusive footer exactly 'IMAGINED · SKY FROM HYDRA'; smaller line 'Terrain, disk appearance and lighting are assumed'. Sober photorealistic scientific illustration, terrain chemistry and fractions unmeasured."
